{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run/draft && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nm=json.load(open('map.json'))\nb2=[b for b in m['behaviors'] if b['id']=='B2-phase1-attributes'][0]\nb2.setdefault('important_branches',[]).append(\\\"with recording enabled the phase-1 entry records metadata for InstanceSpace[r.Id][instance] - the recovering replica's own row - while the new instance is installed under the owner's row, so a recovery-led phase 1 records a different instance or dereferences an absent record; a direct check on this snapshot confirmed a nil pointer dereference when the own row held nothing (claim C9-durable-recorder-uses-the-instance-row, confirmed in scope)\\\")\nb7=[b for b in m['behaviors'] if b['id']=='B7-execute-scheduler'][0]\nb7.setdefault('existing_protections',[]).append(\\\"the per-row timeout enqueues a blocked instance for recovery once the grace period elapses; the direct check for claim C8-timeout-enqueues-blocked-instance confirmed the enqueue (the instance arrived on instancesToRecover after about 12.6 seconds of wall clock), which is the progress path a rejected accept round depends on\\\")\nco=m['core_overview']\nco['open_details'].append(\\\"with recording enabled, the phase-1 entry records metadata through the recovering replica's own row while installing the instance under the owner's row, so a recovery-led phase 1 either records a different instance's ballot context or terminates on an absent record; the direct check for claim C9-durable-recorder-uses-the-instance-row confirmed the nil dereference with Durable true and an empty own row, and the case where that slot exists is still unread (S8-handlePropose-startPhase1, S19-durable-record).\\\")\nco['connection']['explanation']+=\\\" Progress when a round is rejected does not come from the handlers: the direct check for claim C8-timeout-enqueues-blocked-instance confirmed that the executor's per-row timeout enqueues the blocked instance for recovery after roughly twelve seconds of wall clock, so a stalled row is recovered by the timeout path rather than by a rejection signal.\\\"\njson.dump(m,open('map.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nfb={\\\"ref_ids\\\":[\\\"c42c67480b344bf5aed734776a77ab37\\\",\\\"037aa44cdea4453abcd4f9d4439d1dee\\\",\\\"B2-phase1-attributes\\\",\\\"B7-execute-scheduler\\\",\\\"B15-durable-record\\\",\\\"S8-handlePropose-startPhase1\\\",\\\"S19-durable-record\\\",\\\"S4-execute-loop\\\"],\n \\\"answered\\\":\\\"Two confirmed results are recorded at their coordinates. The durability call-site defect (claim C9) is recorded in the phase-1 behavior and as an overview detail: with recording enabled the phase-1 entry records through the recovering replica's own row while installing the instance under the owner's row, which a direct check confirmed panics on an absent record. The executor timeout protection (claim C8) is recorded in the executor behavior's existing protections and in the connection explanation: the enqueue that hands a blocked instance to recovery was confirmed by running the executor (the instance arrived on the recovery channel after about 12.6 seconds), which is the path a rejected round depends on now that the accept-side rejection branch is known to be dead.\\\",\n \\\"remaining\\\":[\\\"the case where the recovering replica's own row holds an instance at that number, where the source implies another instance's metadata would be recorded, is still unread\\\",\n   \\\"the scope-issue bookkeeping on the superseded C1 artifact\\\"],\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Both results are mechanism-level and belong with the behaviors and the overview; the claims and their checks remain the home for the verdicts, and the unread slot-exists case is stated instead of being absorbed into the confirmed claim.\\\",\n \\\"understanding\\\":\\\"updated\\\",\\\"question_updates\\\":{}}\nsub={\\\"action\\\":\\\"research\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Map handoff for the two most recent results: the durability call-site defect (claim C9) and the executor timeout protection (claim C8). Three objects are clarified with sources, with no requirement, binding, edge or identity changes.\\\",\n \\\"map_path\\\":\\\"map.json\\\",\n \\\"map_changes\\\":{\n  \\\"B2-phase1-attributes\\\":{\\\"impact\\\":\\\"clarification\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"A branch records the confirmed wrong-row recording in the phase-1 entry when recording is enabled.\\\",\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S8-handlePropose-startPhase1\\\",\\\"S19-durable-record\\\"],\\\"preserves\\\":\\\"The attribute derivation, the recovery restart and the fact relations of the phase-1 entry are unchanged; the addition is the recording coordinate.\\\"},\n  \\\"B7-execute-scheduler\\\":{\\\"impact\\\":\\\"clarification\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"An existing protection records the confirmed timeout enqueue that hands a blocked instance to recovery.\\\",\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S4-execute-loop\\\",\\\"S14-recovery-start-prepare\\\"],\\\"preserves\\\":\\\"The scan, the watermark advance and the external effects recorded for the executor are unchanged.\\\"},\n  \\\"core_overview\\\":{\\\"impact\\\":\\\"clarification\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The overview gains a sourced open detail for the durability call-site defect and a clause in the connection explanation for the timeout-driven progress path.\\\",\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S8-handlePropose-startPhase1\\\",\\\"S19-durable-record\\\",\\\"S4-execute-loop\\\"],\\\"preserves\\\":\\\"Formation, the rest of context and the existing open details are unchanged.\\\"}},\n \\\"feedback\\\":fb}\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-map-c8c9.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('ok')\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-map-c8c9.json 2>&1 | head -8\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
