ection_injection\": [\"protocol selection: run.go runReplica switch on c.Protocol == epaxos\", \"epaxos.New arguments from run.go: exec = !c.Noop, beacon = false, durable = false, batchWait = 0, transconf = false, failures = (N-1)/2\", \"replica.New hardcodes Thrifty = true, Dreply = true, Beacon = false, Durable = false; epaxos.New then overwrites Beacon and Durable from its own arguments\", \"quorum.conf, latency.conf and aws.conf supply quorum sets and injected per-peer delays (replica/defs/latency.go)\"], \"variants\": [\"N = len(peerAddrList); F = failures; FastQuorumSize = F + (F+1)/2, SlowQuorumSize = (N+1)/2\", \"Thrifty true for the launched configuration\", \"N <= 3 with Thrifty disables the fast-path attribute-equality check\", \"transconf false, Durable false and batching disabled in the launched configuration\"], \"source_ids\": [\"S24-runReplica-epaxos\", \"S1-replica-state\", \"S21-quorum-sizes\", \"S25-defs-channels\"], \"unknowns\": [\"client/buffer.go and client/client.go were not read; the exact completion contract observed by clients (which replies are awaited, what a retry does) is unknown\", \"master/master.go was not read; whether it can change the participant set or the recorded leader while replicas run is unknown\"]}, \"proposed\": {\"system_boundary\": \"Single Go module github.com/imdea-software/swiftpaxos. The audited responsibility is the EPaxos replica package epaxos/ (epaxos.go, defs.go, exec.go) together with the shared replica/, state/ and rpc/ helpers it calls. A replica process is launched by run.go (runReplica) with protocol epaxos; the module also contains sibling protocols (swift, curp, n2paxos, paxos, fastpaxos) that are not part of this run's analysis roots.\", \"protocol_contexts\": [\"epaxos replica process: peer-to-peer RPC over TCP, per-peer reader goroutines, a single run() select loop dispatching Prepare/PreAccept/Accept/Commit/TryPreAccept and their replies\", \"client propose/stat connections handled by replica.client